    "category": "Advanced Querying",
    "difficulty": "Intermediate",
    "readTime": "4 min",
    "summary": "Embed queries inside SELECT, WHERE, and FROM clauses to solve multi-stage data problems.",
    "theory": "A subquery is a query nested inside another statement. Scalar subqueries return a single value (e.g. `WHERE salary > (SELECT AVG(salary) FROM emp)`). Correlated subqueries reference columns from the outer query and evaluate once per outer row.",
    "pro_tip": "Where possible, rewrite correlated subqueries as JOINs or Common Table Expressions (CTEs) for better execution plans.",
    "expected_output": "Employees earning above the departmental average salary identified.",
    "sql_file": "41 SQL Query Sub queries.sql",
    "html_file": "notes/topic-41-subqueries-nested-queries.html",
    "slug": "topic-41-subqueries-nested-queries",
    "raw_sql": "--SUBQUERIES\n\nuse google\n\nselect * from employee\n\n--Find the highest salary \n\nselect max(salary) from employee\n\n\n-- Find the second highest salary \n\nselect max(salary) from employee where salary < (select max(salary) from employee)\n\n--select max(salary) from employee where salary < (130000)\n\n--Find the third highest salary\n\nselect max(salary) from employee where salary <\n(select max(salary) from employee where salary <\n(select max(salary) from employee))\n\n--select max(salary) from employee where salary <\n--98000\n\n--finding fourth highest salary\n\nselect max(salary) from employee where salary <\n(select max(salary) from employee where salary <\n(select max(salary) from employee where salary <\n(select max(salary) from employee)))\n\n\n--Find the Nth highest salary\n\nselect top(5) salary from employee\n\nselect top(5) salary from employee order by salary desc\n\nselect distinct top(5) salary from employee order by salary desc\n\n\nselect min(salary) from employee where salary in \n(select distinct top(5) salary from employee order by salary desc)\n\nselect min(salary) from employee where salary in \n(select distinct top(10) salary from employee order by salary desc)\n\nselect min(salary) from employee where salary in \n(select distinct top(4) salary from employee order by salary desc)\n\n--standard formula\n/*select min(salary) from employee where salary in \n(select distinct top(N) salary from employee order by salary desc)*/\n\nselect * from (select name,salary,dense_rank() \nover (order by salary desc)r from employee) \n as r where r= 8\n\n /*select * from (select name,salary,dense_rank() \nover (order by salary desc)r from employee) \n as r where r= N*/"
